# App version

The product line is **v3**. Source of truth is [lib/appVersion.ts](lib/appVersion.ts).

When you ship user-facing work, bump it in the same change:

- **patch** (`3.2.1`) — bug fix or polish
- **minor** (`3.3.0`) — new feature
- **major** — only if the user asks for a product reset

Also update:

- `package.json` `"version"` to the same number
- `public/sw.js` `CACHE_VERSION` to `pl-predictions-v{number}` so the PWA drops the old shell

Show the label with `APP_VERSION_LABEL` (`v3.2.0`). Do not hardcode `v3.x.x` in UI.
